{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwyAFJ5hGqybPguYv4BZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`vi.mock` doesn't run where you write it. Vitest's transform moves (hoists) every `vi.mock` call to the top of the test file, above the imports, so the mock is registered before the module is imported. That happens even when you write the call inside `beforeEach`.\n\nSo the factory runs at file top, outside your `beforeEach` closure. Any variable it uses from the hook or the surrounding file scope isn't initialized yet, so you get a `ReferenceError`. Vitest wraps that as \"There was an error when mocking a module… make sure there are no top level variables inside, since this call is hoisted to top of the file.\" That message is in your installed copy, in `@vitest/mocker/dist/chunk-registry.js:203`.\n\n**Fixes:**\n- **Same mock for the whole file:** put `vi.mock` at the top level. Create any values the factory needs with `vi.hoisted(() => ...)` so they're hoisted along with it. Then change the mock's behavior per test in `beforeEach`, for example with `vi.mocked(fn).mockReturnValue(...)`.\n- **Mock set up per test:** use `vi.doMock`, which isn't hoisted. Then import the module dynamically (`await import(...)`) after calling it, and call `vi.resetModules()` between tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":291,"cache_read_input_tokens":29287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":291},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22deeaac-242e-4a0e-8a4b-58fe72d4e221","uuid":"7d245edb-5fb3-4537-89a2-16e6b45b7e12","timestamp":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.363Z","request_id":"req_011CfwyAF2TnEjGinqt5j14B"}
